# Transformer Architecture Diagrams

## 1. Complete Transformer Architecture

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Input Processing"
        A[Input Tokens] --> B[Token Embeddings]
        C[Positional Encodings] --> D[Add]
        B --> D
        D --> E[Input Embeddings + Positions]
    end
    
    subgraph "Encoder Stack (N=6 layers)"
        E --> F1[Multi-Head Self-Attention]
        F1 --> F2[Add & Norm]
        E -.Residual.-> F2
        F2 --> F3[Feed Forward Network]
        F3 --> F4[Add & Norm]
        F2 -.Residual.-> F4
        F4 --> F5[Encoder Output]
    end
    
    subgraph "Decoder Stack (N=6 layers)"
        G[Output Tokens Shifted Right] --> H1[Masked Multi-Head Attention]
        H1 --> H2[Add & Norm]
        G -.Residual.-> H2
        H2 --> H3[Cross-Attention]
        F5 -.Encoder Output.-> H3
        H3 --> H4[Add & Norm]
        H2 -.Residual.-> H4
        H4 --> H5[Feed Forward Network]
        H5 --> H6[Add & Norm]
        H4 -.Residual.-> H6
    end
    
    H6 --> I[Linear Layer]
    I --> J[Softmax]
    J --> K[Output Probabilities]
    
    style F1 fill:#e1f5ff
    style H1 fill:#ffe1f5
    style H3 fill:#f5ffe1
```

## 2. Self-Attention Mechanism Detail

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "Input"
        A[Word Embeddings<br/>seq_len × d_model]
    end
    
    subgraph "Linear Projections"
        A --> B[Query<br/>W_Q]
        A --> C[Key<br/>W_K]
        A --> D[Value<br/>W_V]
    end
    
    subgraph "Attention Calculation"
        B --> E[Q · K^T]
        C --> E
        E --> F[Scale by √d_k]
        F --> G[Softmax]
        G --> H[Attention Weights]
        H --> I[Weighted Sum]
        D --> I
    end
    
    I --> J[Attention Output<br/>seq_len × d_model]
    
    style E fill:#ffcccc
    style G fill:#ccffcc
    style I fill:#ccccff
```

## 3. Multi-Head Attention

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Input: seq_len × d_model] --> B[Split into h heads]
    
    subgraph "Head 1"
        B --> C1[Attention<br/>d_k = d_model/h]
    end
    
    subgraph "Head 2"
        B --> C2[Attention<br/>d_k = d_model/h]
    end
    
    subgraph "Head 3"
        B --> C3[Attention<br/>d_k = d_model/h]
    end
    
    subgraph "Head h"
        B --> C4[Attention<br/>d_k = d_model/h]
    end
    
    C1 --> D[Concatenate Heads]
    C2 --> D
    C3 --> D
    C4 --> D
    
    D --> E[Linear Projection]
    E --> F[Output: seq_len × d_model]
    
    style C1 fill:#ff9999
    style C2 fill:#99ff99
    style C3 fill:#9999ff
    style C4 fill:#ffff99
```

## 4. Attention Score Calculation

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Q as Query Matrix
    participant K as Key Matrix
    participant V as Value Matrix
    participant S as Scores
    participant A as Attention Weights
    participant O as Output
    
    Q->>S: Dot product Q · K^T
    K->>S: Transpose and multiply
    S->>S: Scale by √d_k
    S->>A: Apply Softmax
    Note over A: Convert to probabilities<br/>(sum to 1.0)
    A->>O: Multiply with V
    V->>O: Weighted combination
    Note over O: Final contextualized<br/>representation
```

## 5. Encoder vs Decoder Attention

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph "Encoder: Bidirectional Attention"
        E1[Token 1] --> EA[All Tokens]
        E2[Token 2] --> EA
        E3[Token 3] --> EA
        EA --> EO[Full Context]
    end
    
    subgraph "Decoder: Masked Attention"
        D1[Token 1] --> DA1[Token 1 only]
        D2[Token 2] --> DA2[Tokens 1-2]
        D3[Token 3] --> DA3[Tokens 1-3]
        DA1 --> DO[Causal Context]
        DA2 --> DO
        DA3 --> DO
    end
    
    style EA fill:#ccffcc
    style DO fill:#ffcccc
```

## 6. Training Data Flow

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[Training Pair<br/>Source → Target] --> B[Encoder Input:<br/>Full Source]
    A --> C[Decoder Input:<br/>Target Shifted Right]
    A --> D[Decoder Output:<br/>Target]
    
    B --> E[Encoder Processing]
    C --> F[Decoder Processing]
    E --> G[Context Vector]
    G --> F
    
    F --> H[Predictions]
    H --> I[Loss Calculation]
    D --> I
    
    I --> J[Backpropagation]
    J --> K[Update Weights]
    
    style I fill:#ffcccc
    style K fill:#ccffcc
```

## 7. Inference (Generation) Flow

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Start Token] --> B[Decoder]
    B --> C[Predict Next Token]
    C --> D{End Token?}
    D -->|No| E[Append to Sequence]
    E --> B
    D -->|Yes| F[Final Output]
    
    G[Encoder Output<br/>Context] -.-> B
    
    style C fill:#ccffcc
    style D fill:#ffcccc
```

## 8. Positional Encoding Visualization

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "Position Encoding Formula"
        A[Position: pos] --> B[Even dimensions:<br/>sin pos/10000^2i/d_model]
        A --> C[Odd dimensions:<br/>cos pos/10000^2i/d_model]
    end
    
    B --> D[Positional Vector]
    C --> D
    E[Word Embedding] --> F[+]
    D --> F
    F --> G[Input with Position Info]
    
    style D fill:#ffffcc
    style G fill:#ccffff
```

## 9. Attention Pattern Examples

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph "Sentence: The quick brown fox jumps"
        A1[The] -.0.1.-> A1
        A1 -.0.2.-> A2[quick]
        A1 -.0.1.-> A3[brown]
        A1 -.0.5.-> A4[fox]
        A1 -.0.1.-> A5[jumps]
        
        A4 -.0.3.-> A2
        A4 -.0.4.-> A3
        A4 -.0.2.-> A5
    end
    
    Note1[Adjectives attend<br/>to their nouns]
    Note2[Articles attend<br/>to main nouns]
    
    style A4 fill:#ffcccc
    style A2 fill:#ccffcc
    style A3 fill:#ccffcc
```

## 10. Transformer vs RNN Comparison

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph "RNN: Sequential"
        R1[Word 1] --> R2[Hidden State 1]
        R2 --> R3[Word 2] --> R4[Hidden State 2]
        R4 --> R5[Word 3] --> R6[Hidden State 3]
        R6 --> R7[Output]
    end
    
    subgraph "Transformer: Parallel"
        T1[Word 1] --> TA[Self-Attention]
        T2[Word 2] --> TA
        T3[Word 3] --> TA
        TA --> TO[Output All at Once]
    end
    
    style R2 fill:#ffcccc
    style R4 fill:#ffcccc
    style R6 fill:#ffcccc
    style TA fill:#ccffcc
```

